n","conf":"attested","start_date":"1353-12","end_date":"1354-01","note":"dictates the Rihla to Ibn Juzayy (1355)"}],"sources":[{"cite":"Ibn Battuta, Rihla, tr. H. A. R. Gibb and C. F. Beckingham, The Travels of Ibn Battuta (Hakluyt Society, 1958-2000)"},{"cite":"Ross E. Dunn, The Adventures of Ibn Battuta (University of California Press, 1986; rev. 2012)"}],"status":"draft","conf":"estimated"}
{"id":"route:journey:xuanzang","kind":"route","subtype":"journey","name":"Xuanzang's pilgrimage to India","carrier":"person:xuanzang","lenses":["people","geography"],"start":629,"end":645,"what":"Sixteen years (629-645) on foot and horseback from Chang'an to India and back, bringing 657 Buddhist texts.","legs":[{"from":"place:chang_an","to":"place:wuwei","mode":"horse","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0629-08","end_date":"0629-09"},{"from":"place:wuwei","to":"place:guazhou","mode":"horse","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0629-10","end_date":"0629-11"},{"from":"place:guazhou","to":"place:hami","mode":"horse","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0629-12","end_date":"0630-01","note":"crosses the Gobi alone, nearly dies of thirst"},{"from":"place:hami","to":"place:gaochang","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"0630-01","end_date":"0630-02","note":"the king of Turfan begs him to stay; he fasts until released"},{"from":"place:gaochang","to":"place:kucha","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"0630-03","end_date":"0630-04"},{"from":"place:kucha","to":"place:bedel_pass","mode":"foot","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0630-05","end_date":"0630-05","note":"a third of his party dies crossing the Tian Shan"},{"from":"place:bedel_pass","to":"place:suyab","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"0630-05","end_date":"0630-06","note":"meets the Western Turkic khagan"},{"from":"place:suyab","to":"place:tashkent","mode":"horse","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0630-06","end_date":"0630-07"},{"from":"place:tashkent","to":"place:samarkand","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"0630-07","end_date":"0630-08"},{"from":"place:samarkand","to":"place:termez","mode":"horse","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0630-08","end_date":"0630-10"},{"from":"place:termez","to":"place:balkh","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"0630-10","end_date":"0630-11","note":"\"little Rajagriha\", full of monasteries"},{"from":"place:balkh","to":"place:bamiyan_68_35","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"0630-12","end_date":"0631-01","note":"sees the great standing Buddhas"},{"from":"place:bamiyan_68_35","to":"place:kapisa","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"0631-01","end_date":"0631-02"},{"from":"place:kapisa","to":"place:peshawar","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"0631-04","end_date":"0631-05","note":"Kanishka's great stupa"},{"from":"place:peshawar","to":"place:taxila","mode":"foot","conf":"attested","start_date":"0631-06","end_date":"0631-07"},{"from":"place:taxila","to":"place:srinagar","mode":"foot","conf":"attested","start_date":"0631-07","end_date":"0631-09","note":"two years studying in Kashmir"},{"from":"place:srinagar","to":"place:mathura_ancient","mode":"foot","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0633-09","end_date":"0634-06"},{"from":"place:mathura_ancient","to":"place:kanauji","mode":"foot","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0634-07","end_date":"0636-01"},{"from":"place:kanauji","to":"place:shravasti_82_28","mode":"foot","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0636-04","end_date":"0636-07"},{"from":"place:shravasti_82_28","to":"place:kapilavastu","mode":"foot","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0636-07","end_date":"0636-08","note":"the Buddha's home town, in ruins"},{"from":"place:kapilavastu","to":"place:kushinagar","mode":"foot","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0636-08","end_date":"0636-09"},{"from":"place:kushinagar","to":"place:sarnath","mode":"foot","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0636-09","end_date":"0636-10"},{"from":"place:sarnath","to":"place:bodh_gaya","mode":"foot","conf":"attested","start_date":"0636-10","end_date":"0637-01"},{"from":"place:bodh_gaya","to":"place:nalanda","mode":"foot","conf":"attested","start_date":"0637-01","end_date":"0637-02","note":"five years at the great monastery-university under Shilabhadra"},{"from":"place:nalanda","to":"place:kanchipuram","mode":"foot","conf":"approximate","start_date":"0642-01","end_date":"0640-06","note":"tour of south India; order and dates disputed"},{"from":"place:kanchipuram","to":"place:kanauji","mode":"foot","conf":"attested","start_date":"0640-08","end_date":"0643-01","note":"King Harsha's great assembly honours him"},{"from":"place:kanauji","to":"place:prayagraj","mode":"foot","conf":"attested","start_date":"0643-02","end_date":"0643-03","note":"Harsha's quinquennial giving festival"},{"from":"place:prayagraj","to":"place:tashkurgan","mode":"horse","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0643-04","end_date":"0644-03","note":"over the Pamirs, losing an elephant and texts in a river"},{"from":"place:tashkurgan","to":"place:kashgar","mode":"horse","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0644-03","end_date":"0644-04"},{"from":"place:kashgar","to":"place:hotan","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"0644-04","end_date":"0644-05","note":"writes to the emperor asking forgiveness"},{"from":"place:hotan","to":"place:dunhuang","mode":"horse","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0644-12","end_date":"0645-01"},{"from":"place:dunhuang","to":"place:chang_an","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"0645-01","end_date":"0645-02-05","note":"welcomed by crowds; translates for the rest of his life"}],"sources":[{"cite":"Xuanzang, Da Tang Xiyu ji (Great Tang Records on the Western Regions, 646), tr. Li Rongxi (BDK, 1996)"},{"cite":"Sally Hovey Wriggins, The Silk Road Journey with Xuanzang (Westview, 2004)"}],"status":"draft","conf":"attested"}
{"id":"route:journey:marco_polo","kind":"route","subtype":"journey","name":"Marco Polo's journey to Kublai Khan","carrier":"person:marco_polo","lenses":["people","geography"],"start":1271,"end":1295,"what":"With his father Niccolò and uncle Maffeo: Venice to the Mongol court and back by sea (1271-1295).","legs":[{"from":"place:venice","to":"place:acre","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1271","end_date":"1271","note":"carries a letter from the new pope, Gregory X"},{"from":"place:acre","to":"place:aegae_9377","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1271-11","end_date":"1271-12","note":"Laiazzo in Cilician Armenia"},{"from":"place:aegae_9377","to":"place:tabriz","mode":"caravan","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1271-12","end_date":"1272-03"},{"from":"place:tabriz","to":"place:kerman","mode":"caravan","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1272-03","end_date":"1272-06"},{"from":"place:kerman","to":"place:hormuz","mode":"caravan","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1272-06","end_date":"1272-08","note":"the ships look unsafe; they turn north overland"},{"from":"place:hormuz","to":"place:balkh","mode":"caravan","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1272-08","end_date":"1273-01"},{"from":"place:balkh","to":"place:badakhshan","mode":"horse","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1273-01","end_date":"1273-02","note":"a year in the mountains recovering from illness"},{"from":"place:badakhshan","to":"place:kashgar","mode":"horse","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1274-01","end_date":"1274-04","note":"over the Pamirs"},{"from":"place:kashgar","to":"place:hotan","mode":"caravan","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1274-04","end_date":"1274-06"},{"from":"place:hotan","to":"place:dunhuang","mode":"caravan","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1274-06","end_date":"1274-10","note":"Shazhou, after the Lop desert"},{"from":"place:dunhuang","to":"place:zhangye","mode":"caravan","conf":"approximate","start_date":"1274-10","end_date":"1274-11","note":"Ganzhou; he says they stayed a year"},{"from":"place:zhangye","to":"place:xanadu","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"1275-03","end_date":"1275-05","note":"Xanadu, Kublai's summer capital"},{"from":"place:xanadu","to":"place:khanbaliq","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"1275-08","end_date":"1275-09","note":"seventeen years in Kublai Khan's service"},{"from":"place:khanbaliq","to":"place:kunming","mode":"horse","conf":"approximate","start_date":"1290-12","end_date":"1280","note":"mission to Yunnan (Carajan); date uncertain"},{"from":"place:kunming","to":"place:hangzhou","mode":"river","conf":"approximate","start_date":"1280","end_date":"1285","note":"Quinsai, \"the finest city in the world\""},{"from":"place:hangzhou","to":"place:quanzhou","mode":"river","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1285","end_date":"1291-01","note":"sails with 14 ships escorting the princess Kököchin to Persia"},{"from":"place:quanzhou","to":"place:pasai","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1291-01","end_date":"1291-04","note":"five months on Sumatra waiting for the monsoon"},{"from":"place:pasai","to":"place:colombo","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1291-09","end_date":"1291-11"},{"from":"place:colombo","to":"place:hormuz","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1291-11","end_date":"1293-02","note":"of 600 passengers, 18 survive the voyage"},{"from":"place:hormuz","to":"place:tabriz","mode":"horse","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1293-02","end_date":"1293-05","note":"nine months at the Ilkhan's court"},{"from":"place:tabriz","to":"place:trebizond","mode":"horse","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1294-01","end_date":"1294-04","note":"robbed of much of their fortune"},{"from":"place:trebizond","to":"place:constantinople","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1294-04","end_date":"1295-01"},{"from":"place:constantinople","to":"place:venice","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1295-01","end_date":"1295","note":"home after 24 years; later a prisoner in Genoa (1298-99), where he tells the tale"}],"sources":[{"cite":"Marco Polo and Rustichello da Pisa, Le Devisement du monde (c.1300), tr. Sharon Kinoshita (Hackett, 2016)"},{"cite":"Hans Ulrich Vogel, Marco Polo Was in China (Brill, 2013)"}],"status":"draft","conf":"estimated"}
{"id":"route:journey:mansa_musa","kind":"route","subtype":"journey","name":"Mansa Musa's hajj","carrier":"person:musa_i_of_mali","lenses":["people","geography"],"start":1324,"end":1325,"what":"The ruler of Mali crosses the Sahara with a vast caravan and gives away so much gold in Cairo that its price falls for years (1324-1325).","legs":[{"from":"place:niani","to":"place:oualata","mode":"caravan","conf":"approximate","start_date":"1324-01","end_date":"1324-03"},{"from":"place:oualata","to":"place:tuat","mode":"caravan","conf":"approximate","start_date":"1324-03","end_date":"1324-04","note":"oasis route; some say via Ghadames"},{"from":"place:tuat","to":"place:cairo","mode":"caravan","conf":"attested","start_date":"1324-04","end_date":"1324-07","note":"refuses to bow to the Mamluk sultan; floods Cairo with gold"},{"from":"place:cairo","to":"place:mecca","mode":"caravan","conf":"attested","start_date":"1324-10","end_date":"1324-11","note":"performs the hajj"},{"from":"place:mecca","to":"place:cairo","mode":"caravan","conf":"attested","start_date":"1324-12","end_date":"1325-02","note":"returns having borrowed money: his gold ran out"},{"from":"place:cairo","to":"place:timbuktu","mode":"caravan","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1325-03","end_date":"1325-08","note":"commissions the Djinguereber mosque, with the poet-architect al-Sahili"},{"from":"place:timbuktu","to":"place:gao","mode":"river","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1325-08","end_date":"1325-09"}],"sources":[{"cite":"al-Umari, Masalik al-absar (c.1340), in N. Levtzion and J. F. P. Hopkins, Corpus of Early Arabic Sources for West African History (CUP, 1981)"},{"cite":"Michael A. Gomez, African Dominion (Princeton, 2018), ch. 6-7"}],"status":"draft","conf":"estimated"}
{"id":"route:journey:faxian","kind":"route","subtype":"journey","name":"Faxian's pilgrimage to India","carrier":"person:faxian","lenses":["people","geography"],"start":399,"end":414,"what":"A Chinese monk walks to India for monastic rules and sails home via Sri Lanka and Java (399-414).","legs":[{"from":"place:chang_an","to":"place:dunhuang","mode":"foot","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0399","end_date":"0400","note":"\"no birds above, no beasts below\" in the desert"},{"from":"place:dunhuang","to":"place:shanshan","mode":"foot","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0400","end_date":"0400"},{"from":"place:shanshan","to":"place:hotan","mode":"foot","conf":"attested","start_date":"0400","end_date":"0401","note":"watches the great image procession"},{"from":"place:hotan","to":"place:mingora","mode":"foot","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0401","end_date":"0402","note":"Udyana, over the Pamirs and the Indus gorges"},{"from":"place:mingora","to":"place:peshawar","mode":"foot","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0402","end_date":"0402"},{"from":"place:peshawar","to":"place:mathura_ancient","mode":"foot","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0403","end_date":"0403"},{"from":"place:mathura_ancient","to":"place:shravasti_82_28","mode":"foot","conf":"estimated","start_date":"0404","end_date":"0404"},{"from":"place:shravasti_82_28","to":"place:pataliputra_ancient","mode":"foot","conf":"attested","start_date":"0404","end_date":"0405","note":"three years learning Sanskrit and copying the Vinaya"},{"from":"place:pataliputra_ancient","to":"place:tamralipti","mode":"foot","conf":"attested","start_date":"0408","end_date":"0408","note":"two years copying sutras"},{"from":"place:tamralipti","to":"place:anuradhapura","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"0410","end_date":"0410","note":"weeps at a Chinese silk fan offered at a shrine"},{"from":"place:anuradhapura","to":"place:semarang","mode":"sea","conf":"approximate","start_date":"0412","end_date":"0412","note":"Yepoti: Java or Borneo; a storm drives the ship off course"},{"from":"place:semarang","to":"place:laoshan","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"0413","end_date":"0413","note":"lands on the Shandong coast, far north of his goal"},{"from":"place:laoshan","to":"place:jiankang","mode":"land","conf":"attested","start_date":"0413","end_date":"0414","note":"Nanjing; writes his record and translates"}],"sources":[{"cite":"Faxian, Foguo ji (Record of Buddhist Kingdoms, 416), tr. James Legge (Oxford, 1886)"},{"cite":"Max Deeg, Das Gaoseng-Faxian-Zhuan als religionsgeschichtliche Quelle (Harrassowitz, 2005)"}],"status":"draft","conf":"estimated"}
{"id":"route:journey:zheng_he_1405","kind":"route","subtype":"journey","name":"Zheng He's first treasure voyage","carrier":"person:zheng_he","lenses":["people","geography"],"start":1405,"end":1407,"what":"About 27,800 men in some 250 ships sail from the Ming court to Calicut and back (1405-1407).","legs":[{"from":"place:nanjing","to":"place:liujiagang","mode":"river","conf":"attested","start_date":"1405-07","end_date":"1405-07","note":"the fleet gathers at the Yangzi mouth"},{"from":"place:liujiagang","to":"place:qui_nhon","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1405-10","end_date":"1406-01","note":"Champa"},{"from":"place:qui_nhon","to":"place:surabaya","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1406-01","end_date":"1406-03","note":"Majapahit Java; 170 of his men killed in a civil war"},{"from":"place:surabaya","to":"place:palembang","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1406-03","end_date":"1406-05"},{"from":"place:palembang","to":"place:malacca","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1406-05","end_date":"1406-06"},{"from":"place:malacca","to":"place:pasai","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1406-06","end_date":"1406-08"},{"from":"place:pasai","to":"place:galle","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1406-08","end_date":"1406-11"},{"from":"place:galle","to":"place:calicut","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1406-11","end_date":"1406-12","note":"turnaround; erects a stele"},{"from":"place:calicut","to":"place:palembang","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1407-04","end_date":"1407-06","note":"defeats the pirate Chen Zuyi"},{"from":"place:palembang","to":"place:nanjing","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1407-06","end_date":"1407-10-02","note":"presents Chen Zuyi for execution"}],"sources":[{"cite":"Ma Huan, Yingya Shenglan (1433), tr. J. V. G. Mills (Hakluyt Society, 1970)"},{"cite":"Edward L. Dreyer, Zheng He: China and the Oceans in the Early Ming Dynasty (Pearson, 2007)"}],"status":"draft","conf":"estimated"}
{"id":"route:journey:zheng_he_1417","kind":"route","subtype":"journey","name":"Zheng He's fifth voyage, to Africa","carrier":"person:zheng_he","lenses":["people","geography"],"start":1417,"end":1419,"what":"The treasure fleet reaches Arabia and the Swahili coast and brings a giraffe to the Ming court (1417-1419).","legs":[{"from":"place:nanjing","to":"place:quanzhou","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1417-05","end_date":"1417-06","note":"prays at the Muslim tombs"},{"from":"place:quanzhou","to":"place:qui_nhon","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1417-06","end_date":"1417-12"},{"from":"place:qui_nhon","to":"place:malacca","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1417-12","end_date":"1418-01"},{"from":"place:malacca","to":"place:calicut","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1418-01","end_date":"1418-03"},{"from":"place:calicut","to":"place:hormuz","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1418-03","end_date":"1418-04"},{"from":"place:hormuz","to":"place:aden","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1418-04","end_date":"1418-05"},{"from":"place:aden","to":"place:mogadishu","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1418-05","end_date":"1418-08"},{"from":"place:mogadishu","to":"place:malindi","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1418-08","end_date":"1418-09","note":"envoys with giraffes (the qilin) join the fleet"},{"from":"place:malindi","to":"place:nanjing","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1418-10","end_date":"1419-08-08"}],"sources":[{"cite":"Edward L. Dreyer, Zheng He: China and the Oceans in the Early Ming Dynasty (Pearson, 2007)"},{"cite":"Liujiagang and Changle steles of 1431, tr. in Dreyer 2007, appendix"}],"status":"draft","conf":"attested"}
{"id":"route:journey:zheng_he_1431","kind":"route","subtype":"journey","name":"Zheng He's seventh and last voyage","carrier":"person:zheng_he","lenses":["people","geography"],"start":1431,"end":1433,"what":"The last treasure fleet; a squadron reaches Mecca; Zheng He dies on the way home (1431-1433).","legs":[{"from":"place:nanjing","to":"place:changle","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1431-01-19","end_date":"1431-04","note":"carves the stele that lists all seven voyages"},{"from":"place:changle","to":"place:qui_nhon","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1431-12","end_date":"1432-01"},{"from":"place:qui_nhon","to":"place:surabaya","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1432-01","end_date":"1432-03"},{"from":"place:surabaya","to":"place:malacca","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1432-07","end_date":"1432-07"},{"from":"place:malacca","to":"place:calicut","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1432-08","end_date":"1432-12","note":"Ma Huan's squadron goes on to Jeddah and Mecca"},{"from":"place:calicut","to":"place:hormuz","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1432-12","end_date":"1433-01"},{"from":"place:hormuz","to":"place:calicut","mode":"sea","conf":"approximate","start_date":"1433-03","end_date":"1433-04","note":"Zheng He probably dies here or at sea, spring 1433"},{"from":"place:calicut","to":"place:nanjing","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1433-04","end_date":"1433-07-22","note":"the fleet returns; the voyages end"}],"sources":[{"cite":"Edward L. Dreyer, Zheng He: China and the Oceans in the Early Ming Dynasty (Pearson, 2007)"},{"cite":"Ma Huan, Yingya Shenglan (1433), tr. J. V. G. Mills (Hakluyt Society, 1970)"}],"status":"draft","conf":"attested"}
{"id":"route:journey:evliya_celebi","kind":"route","subtype":"journey","name":"Evliya Çelebi's travels","carrier":"person:evliya_celebi","lenses":["people","geography"],"start":1640,"end":1672,"what":"Forty years across the Ottoman world and beyond, written up in the ten-volume Seyahatname (1640-1682).","legs":[{"from":"place:istanbul","to":"place:bursa","mode":"land","conf":"attested","start_date":"1640","end_date":"1640"},{"from":"place:bursa","to":"place:trabzon","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1640","end_date":"1640"},{"from":"place:trabzon","to":"place:bakhchiserai","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1641","end_date":"1641","note":"the Crimean Khan's court"},{"from":"place:bakhchiserai","to":"place:istanbul","mode":"sea","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1641","end_date":"1642"},{"from":"place:istanbul","to":"place:erzurum","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"1645","end_date":"1646","note":"in the governor's service"},{"from":"place:erzurum","to":"place:tabriz","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"1648","end_date":"1647","note":"embassy to Safavid Persia"},{"from":"place:tabriz","to":"place:damascus","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"1647","end_date":"1648"},{"from":"place:damascus","to":"place:sarajevo","mode":"horse","conf":"estimated","start_date":"1650","end_date":"1660"},{"from":"place:sarajevo","to":"place:vienna","mode":"horse","conf":"attested","start_date":"1660","end_date":"1665","note":"with the Ottoman embassy of Kara Mehmed Pasha"},{"from":"place:vienna","to":"place:heraklion","mode":"sea","conf":"attested","start_date":"1665","end_date":"1667","note":"at the siege of Candia, Crete"},{"from":"place:heraklion","to":"place:mecca","mode":"caravan","conf":"attested","start_date":"1669","end_date":"1671","note":"the hajj"},{"from":"place:mecca","to":"place:cairo","mode":"caravan","conf":"attested","start_date":"1672","end_date":"1672","note":"settles in Cairo; travels up the Nile to Sudan (1672-73